# CASM Phase 13 WP82 trusted reference: casmincbin1
#
# Independently hand-assembled from the casmincbin1 fixture source in
# cmake/GenerateCasmTestFixtures.cmake. NOT produced by CASM. Proves
# .INCBIN streams a real binary asset's bytes verbatim through the real
# production parser/emitter (parser.s's ppsIncbin, emit.s's emitIncbin).
#
# Source (.ORG $C000, fixed address):
#   .ORG $C000
#   .INCBIN "CASMINCBIN1.DAT"
#
# Filename is uppercase in source text (plain ASCII bytes $43 $41 $53...).
# cc1541 -f encodes a lowercase-typed argument as unshifted PETSCII
# (numerically identical to uppercase ASCII) but an uppercase-typed
# argument as shifted/bit-7-set PETSCII -- confirmed live via cc1541 -a's
# own reconstruction of a first, failed attempt. CMakeLists.txt's own
# packaging command therefore passes -f "casmincbin1.dat" (lowercase) to
# get the byte-matching unshifted encoding, same established pairing as
# this project's existing .INCLUDE fixtures (CASMFRC1/CASMFRC2 in source
# text, "casmfrc1"/"casmfrc2" lowercase as their own -f arguments).
#
# tests/fixtures/casm/casmincbin1.dat is a real 4-byte binary asset, bytes
# DE AD BE EF (independently verified: xxd tests/fixtures/casm/
# casmincbin1.dat), packaged onto casm_phase13_test_d64 under a directory
# name that is byte-identical to this source's own quoted filename string.
#
# Hand assembly:
#   00 C0        PRG load-address header ($C000, little-endian)
#   DE AD BE EF  .INCBIN "CASMINCBIN1.DAT" (verbatim file contents)
#
# bytes: 6

00 C0
DE AD BE EF
